\details{
Boruta is an all-relevant selector: it looks for every feature that carries
information about the target, rather than the smallest subset that predicts
best. Redundant but informative features are therefore all confirmed, which
helps you understand a dataset more than it helps you build a compact
model. The search costs up to \code{maxRuns} random-forest fits, and its
outcome varies from run to run unless \code{seed} is supplied. The forests are
grown on a single thread (\code{num.threads = 1} is passed to Boruta's
importance source), in line with featR's sequential default.

Features still undecided when \code{maxRuns} is reached are Tentative.
\code{resolve_tentative = TRUE} settles them with the
\code{Boruta::TentativeRoughFix()} heuristic, not with further evidence. The
heuristic confirms a tentative feature whenever its median importance
